<Layout title="Take Folklore into Codex — Folklore"><article class="prose-page"><h1>The field guide,<br/>where you build.</h1><p class="lede">An offline catalog of 30 UI elements and 10 visual styles. Bring the vocabulary, anatomy, and implementation notes into Codex.</p><div class="download-options"><a href="/downloads/folklore-plugin-1.0.0.zip" download>Download plugin<span>Codex package · v1.0.0 · ZIP</span></a><a href="/downloads/folklore-skill-1.0.0.zip" download>Download standalone skill<span>Portable SKILL.md · v1.0.0 · ZIP</span></a></div><h2>Install the standalone skill</h2><ol><li>Download and extract the skill archive. It contains a folder named <code>folklore</code>.</li><li>For a project, place that folder in <code>.agents/skills/</code> at the repository root. For personal use, place it in <code>~/.agents/skills/</code>.</li><li>Start a new Codex session and invoke <code>$folklore</code>. Node.js 18 or newer is needed for the lookup commands; the Markdown references can be read without it.</li></ol><p>Example request:</p><pre><code>Use $folklore to name the dark layer behind my popup, explain its parts, and help me build it in this project.</code></pre><h2>Use the plugin package</h2><p>The plugin bundles the same skill with a Codex compatibility manifest. Extract it into a local plugin source, add it to a local or repository marketplace, and install from that source in a supporting Codex desktop surface. This download is not a listing in the public plugin directory.</p><p><a href="https://developers.openai.com/plugins/build/plugins">Current OpenAI plugin installation and packaging guidance</a> explains the marketplace format and supported surfaces. The repository includes a marketplace example in <code>examples/marketplace.json</code>.</p><h2>Look things up locally</h2><p>From the extracted <code>folklore</code> skill directory:</p><pre><code>node scripts/lookup.mjs search "gray shapes before content loads"
node scripts/lookup.mjs get skeleton
node scripts/lookup.mjs compare skeleton spinner
node scripts/lookup.mjs search "frosted cards" --kind style</code></pre><h2>What the skill does</h2><p>It identifies likely patterns, distinguishes neighboring concepts, explains anatomy and platform vocabulary, and adapts build or debug briefs to your project. Search scores rank matches; they are not confidence percentages.</p><h2>Versioned, inspectable, offline</h2><p>No API key, account, or hosted service is required. Installation does not send project files to Folklore. The host coding agent continues to operate under its own data and permission settings. Updating the catalog means installing a newer release.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/Parthawe/folklore-ui">Read the source and release notes on GitHub</a>.</p></article></Layout>
